[Music]  you've likely heard the story of lucifer  the fallen angel according to christian  legend  lucifer was the most senior and most  beautiful angel in god's heavenly court  he wanted to be more powerful than god  and rebelled along with some other  corrupted angels  after ensuing heavenly war lucifer and  other angels were banished from heaven  and descended all the way down to hell  lucifer now a fallen angel became the  devil  his fellow fallen angels became demons  okay with me so far good the story you  just heard  is not in the bible well at least not in  the way it's often  told the real origin of lucifer is a lot  more interesting  it's actually one of misinformation  conflation  and one very curious mistranslation  let me explain before we get into wars  in heaven  fallen angels and hellfire let's start  with his name  lucifer it's just one of many names used  for the devil  like satan and the beast and those names  are used quite a lot of times in the  bible  but only once is the name lucifer ever  mentioned  and that's in the old testament's book  of isaiah in chapter 14 verse 12 of the  book  the prophet isaiah says this how you are  fallen from heaven o lucifer  son of the morning how you are cut down  to the ground  you who weakened the nations even though  the name lucifer is mentioned  this taunting remark is actually  directed towards the arrogant king of  babylon  whose kingdom had just been destroyed  isaiah is basically teasing him for it  so how you fallen o lucifer's son of the  morning  kind of just means king of babylon oh  look how the mighty have fallen  but why did isaiah need to call him  lucifer what satan got to do with any of  this  well you might say lucifer was  ungraciously cast down from heaven as  well  so likening the king of babylon to  lucifer is actually a pretty good  comparison here  and yes you would be right but the thing  is  if you examine the text in its original  language isaiah  was never really making this comparison  in the first place  when we read the same text in its  original language biblical hebrew  isaiah's taunt actually sounds a bit  like this eknapalta mishamayim hail  benjakha  did you hear me say the word lucifer no  nowhere does the real isaiah actually  say this name instead it be called  lucifer  the king of babylon is called he'll be  literally a shining one son of morning  in hebrew  a shining one son of morning does not  refer to satan or the devil  but a planet the planet venus otherwise  known as the morning star  besides the moon venus is the brightest  body in the night sky  and because it's so bright it's often  the first star  that can be seen in the evening and the  last star you can see when the sun comes  up  hence the name the morning star or in  hebrew  shining one son of mourning  so back to isaiah is taunted about the  morning star and it all begins to make  sense if applied to the planet venus  by describing the king of babylon as o  shining one son of morning  isaiah is likening the king's epic fall  from grace to the movement of the  morning star  which every morning appears to fall from  the sky into the underworld  in the sumerian religions of ancient  iraq the goddess inanna  was associated with the planet venus  there are several hymns of praise to  inanna in a role as the goddess the  planet  but a particularly famous hymn inanna's  descent to the underworld  describes how unlike any other deity  inanna is able to fall from heaven  descend into the netherworld and rise  back the next day  just like the planet venus does every  dusk and dawn  we've established that isaiah is  actually talking about the movements of  the morning star the planet venus  but how on earth did it become lucifer  well once the bible was translated to  latin by early christians  they came across isaiah 14 12 and  translated the hebrew word from  morningstar  into their own word for morningstar  lucifer  lucifer is a latin word for morningstar  with a word literally translating to  lightbringer in greco-roman myth  the morning star was often personified  and considered a god  and in some myths considered to be the  son of aurora  the dawn how did the star  lucifer aka venus turn so evil  and where do the fallen angels come in  to thank for that  you have the book of enoch it's an  apocryphal biblical text  written around 300-200 bce and it didn't  quite make it into the final cut of the  bible  but was incredibly popular in second  temple judaism in the book of enoch  there's a chapter called  the book of watchers and in this chapter  we have the watchers  who were dispatched to earth to watch  over humanity  but they did a terrible terrible job and  they soon began to lust for human women  and led by their leader samyaza all  started to defect from god's command  and began to procreate among human women  the offspring are called the nephilim or  giants who pillaged the earth and  endangered humanity  samyaza and his fallen angel cronies  also began to teach the humans certain  forbidden arts like weaponry cosmetics  mirrors sorceries and other hidden  secrets  meanwhile god's looking down in anger  and disbelief  so allows a great flood to rid the earth  of the corrupted humankind and those  nephilim  but first warning noah to build his ark  as described in the book of genesis  afterwards he gets his loyal angels to  punish the fallen watchers  including their evil leader samyaza  [Music]  remember none of this is actually canon  for mainstream christianity or judaism  it's labeled as an apocryphal book in  today's terms  that's the equivalent of being a sort of  bible fan fiction  but at the time people loved the book of  enoch so much  that it began to influence contemporary  religious ideas  even in the new testament book of jude  the book of enoch is directly quoted  around the time of enoch circulation  jews and early christians  rummaged through the old testament to  see if they'd missed any hidden secrets  and they just so happened to stumble on  a little verse in the book of isaiah  instead of seeing it as a reference to  the planet venus as originally intended  they found a hidden reference to that  fallen angel samyaza as seen in the book  of enoch  and when early christians read isaiah  and latin they came to understand  lucifer not as lightbringer but as a  name  a name for a fallen angel and so  lucifer the name for the fallen angel  finally stuck  and was added to a growing number of  names used for the devil such as satan  the beast beelzebub and so on now each  one of those names have their own  fascinating origins that i'd love to  cover in a future video  but for now i'll leave it to that  and that is as close of an origin story  to lucifer  as we can get it's the story of our  planet accidentally became a fallen  angel  today's bibles no longer use lucifer in  their translations  and instead use morningstar in isaiah 14  12.  the story of how lucifer got his name is  such a rabbit hole so i recommend to  explore the topic yourself  as with all my videos i've provided  links down below  if you're new here while i subscribe i  have a series of videos on my channel  that might interest you  anyway i look forward to seeing you  again for my next video  goodbye

